{:edb/db-before-t 2141 :edb/db-after-t 2142 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535454 50 #inst "2026-10-09T00:26:32.389Z" 13194139535454 true] [17592186068688 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349977 13194139535454 true] [17592186078311 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349984 13194139535454 true] [17592186092130 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349956 13194139535454 true] [17592186100867 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349963 13194139535454 true] [17592186110579 1020 #edb/ref 17592186350005 13194139535454 true] [17592186120123 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535454 true] [17592186120123 1100 "If $h(x) = \\sqrt{2x + 3}$, find $(h^{-1})^{′}(x)$ as a function of $h^{-1}(x)$." 13194139535454 false] [17592186120123 1100 "If $h(x)=\\sqrt{2x+3},$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186120123 1145 "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=\\sqrt{2x+3},$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2y+3}\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[\\sqrt{2y+3}] \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[(2y+3)^{1/2}] \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =(2y+3)^{-1/2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2y+3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{2y+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+3} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186124583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349991 13194139535454 true] [17592186157374 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349998 13194139535454 true] [17592186175827 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349970 13194139535454 true] [17592186349956 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349957 13194139535454 true] [17592186349956 1089 "q-11981" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349956 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535454 true] [17592186349956 1100 "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=4 \\\\ 2x-y=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349956 1113 #uuid "e2ae4a2f-fd5f-5872-89b2-269b37fd8b57" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349956 1145 "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349958 13194139535454 true] [17592186349957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349959 13194139535454 true] [17592186349957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349960 13194139535454 true] [17592186349957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349961 13194139535454 true] [17592186349957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349962 13194139535454 true] [17592186349957 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535454 true] [17592186349957 1041 "selection" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349957 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349961 13194139535454 true] [17592186349957 1110 #uuid "eef2c23a-5001-5982-b0f4-845efea30bc2" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349958 1034 "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349958 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349958 1111 #uuid "b435961a-37d4-5224-ba98-809edcd5fcfa" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349959 1034 "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349959 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349959 1111 #uuid "d6d04f0e-ce33-560f-8d25-2455198c422e" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349960 1034 "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349960 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349960 1111 #uuid "b6629edf-3d57-548c-9714-d3922342714c" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349961 1034 "x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349961 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349961 1111 #uuid "8e6b3535-dc3e-5474-8344-c9298e897403" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349962 1034 "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349962 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349962 1111 #uuid "24ddd589-010f-5889-9e7d-826aef99668e" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349963 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349964 13194139535454 true] [17592186349963 1089 "q-121028" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349963 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535454 true] [17592186349963 1100 "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{8}+n\\pi ,\\,x=a\\pi +n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349963 1113 #uuid "48581854-707a-55c3-820d-b972a1199e65" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349963 1145 "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & 2x=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & 2x=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}+n\\pi , & \\, & \\, & x=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}+n\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=\\frac{7}{8}.$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349965 13194139535454 true] [17592186349964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349966 13194139535454 true] [17592186349964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349967 13194139535454 true] [17592186349964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349968 13194139535454 true] [17592186349964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349969 13194139535454 true] [17592186349964 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535454 true] [17592186349964 1041 "selection" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349964 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349966 13194139535454 true] [17592186349964 1110 #uuid "efe4347c-0b67-51e7-a55f-d6c7fdd8f093" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349965 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349965 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349965 1111 #uuid "3a4d3a07-a231-521c-a426-1cd6cd9993d8" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349966 1034 "\\frac{7}{8}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349966 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349966 1111 #uuid "4b008d64-98cd-5cf1-970e-5ef9d2d8acba" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349967 1034 "\\frac{5}{8}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349967 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349967 1111 #uuid "739b2b03-cec2-56b5-aa38-4ace4bc119c8" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349968 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349968 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349968 1111 #uuid "1bd67f70-d6c2-5071-b7e4-83c5f5974917" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349969 1034 "\\frac{3}{8}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349969 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349969 1111 #uuid "84139496-dd2c-5b40-a558-029ab7fa76e6" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349970 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349971 13194139535454 true] [17592186349970 1089 "q-129223" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349970 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535454 true] [17592186349970 1100 "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y=\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{x}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}?$   \n\n- $[-1,1]$\n- $[-2,2]$\n- $[0,1]$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349970 1113 #uuid "b4e4bfc1-b5ef-51c2-a12a-529f7a844a95" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349970 1145 "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous. \n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The intervals $[-1,1]$ and $[0,1]$ are closed, and the function is continuous on each of these intervals. Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable on each $[-1,1]$  and $[0,1].$\n\n- The interval $[-2,2]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on it because it is not defined at $x=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139535454 true] [17592186349971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349972 13194139535454 true] [17592186349971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349973 13194139535454 true] [17592186349971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349974 13194139535454 true] [17592186349971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349975 13194139535454 true] [17592186349971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349976 13194139535454 true] [17592186349971 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535454 true] [17592186349971 1041 "selection" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349971 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349973 13194139535454 true] [17592186349971 1110 #uuid "1afb4ca5-ca86-55ee-a9f9-e8dc94611ae5" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349972 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349972 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535454 true] [17592186349972 1111 #uuid "20fde7ef-7f23-585a-b164-e9d1afdcb361" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349973 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349973 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535454 true] [17592186349973 1111 #uuid "53025eaa-e03c-5a79-9f02-e480ce97b82f" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349974 1034 "I only" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349974 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535454 true] [17592186349974 1111 #uuid "c9864dd8-11c3-550d-9dac-a1977ebd9c6d" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349975 1034 "III only" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349975 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535454 true] [17592186349975 1111 #uuid "15c9a850-725f-517a-bc3d-861d44c558ae" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349976 1034 "None" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349976 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535454 true] [17592186349976 1111 #uuid "27415501-96b9-5193-84c6-f9cb710b1f02" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349977 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349978 13194139535454 true] [17592186349977 1089 "q-14432" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349977 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535454 true] [17592186349977 1100 "$\\frac{4}{5g}÷\\frac{3}{10{g}^{2}}=$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349977 1113 #uuid "53d8f5ac-4e03-5656-9b30-96c599c40d3e" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349977 1145 "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5g}÷\\frac{3}{10{g}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5g}÷\\frac{3}{10{g}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{5g}\\cdot \\frac{10{g}^{2}}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\cancel{5}\\cdot \\cancel{g}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{5}\\cdot 2\\cdot {g}^{\\cancel{2}}}{3} & = \\\\ 4\\cdot \\frac{2g}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{8g}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349979 13194139535454 true] [17592186349978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349980 13194139535454 true] [17592186349978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349981 13194139535454 true] [17592186349978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349982 13194139535454 true] [17592186349978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349983 13194139535454 true] [17592186349978 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535454 true] [17592186349978 1041 "selection" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349978 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349983 13194139535454 true] [17592186349978 1110 #uuid "ed517a1f-0582-5bc2-a1f9-34e84174f8be" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349979 1034 "\\frac{4g}{15}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349979 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349979 1111 #uuid "00271db1-ce5d-5870-8ecf-b3d687ff0c03" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349980 1034 "\\frac{5}{2g}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349980 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349980 1111 #uuid "4b40eec7-3fcc-5c08-b260-edea6a6b44ba" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349981 1034 "\\frac{4{g}^{2}}{3}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349981 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349981 1111 #uuid "b6a3cdc3-89a3-56cd-8306-b29ea372c374" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349982 1034 "\\frac{6}{g}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349982 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349982 1111 #uuid "88dde628-02bf-5a93-b478-e0e0085e04a2" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349983 1034 "\\frac{8g}{3}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349983 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349983 1111 #uuid "d12cb98d-88b6-589d-8446-4a8b8393d644" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349984 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349985 13194139535454 true] [17592186349984 1089 "q-15459" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349984 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535454 true] [17592186349984 1100 "A circle in the Cartesian plane is given by the equation ${y}^{2}+2x+{x}^{2}=24y-120.$ If the circle is written in the standard form $(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2},$ then $a+b+r=$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349984 1113 #uuid "1c7ac090-4865-5789-a9b9-f3f3d9345ee3" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349984 1145 "To find the standard form $(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2},$ we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+2x+{x}^{2} & =24y-120 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x+{y}^{2}-24y & =-120 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x)+({y}^{2}-24y) & =-120 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 12y+{12}^{2}) & =-120+{1}^{2}+{12}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 12y+{12}^{2}) & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+(y-12)^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-12)^{2} & ={5}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-1,b=12,r=5,$ and \n\n$$\na+b+r=-1+12+5=16.\n$$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349986 13194139535454 true] [17592186349985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349987 13194139535454 true] [17592186349985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349988 13194139535454 true] [17592186349985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349989 13194139535454 true] [17592186349985 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349990 13194139535454 true] [17592186349985 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535454 true] [17592186349985 1041 "selection" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349985 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349988 13194139535454 true] [17592186349985 1110 #uuid "5eb7b41d-1ff5-5dcf-b3d4-1f415821afa2" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349986 1034 "12" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349986 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349986 1111 #uuid "b15bc5f6-b521-570b-977c-4ec6cb64f4ae" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349987 1034 "10" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349987 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349987 1111 #uuid "4d474441-f83d-5751-960e-48d3a449323e" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349988 1034 "16" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349988 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349988 1111 #uuid "9a8ec8fd-ce2d-5eb3-8db9-45c6f17be030" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349989 1034 "15" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349989 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349989 1111 #uuid "a3271490-7360-5c33-8f48-b80e2a4eb53f" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349990 1034 "14" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349990 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186349990 1111 #uuid "be1edce8-9456-501a-beba-6ccc30f01c50" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349991 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349992 13194139535454 true] [17592186349991 1089 "q-68043" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349991 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535454 true] [17592186349991 1100 "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{3}+x}{2{x}^{2}+x+4}.$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349991 1113 #uuid "f2188e54-85fe-53d7-875d-fe88e450703e" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349991 1145 "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{3}+x}{2{x}^{2}+x+4} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(x+\\frac{1}{x})}{(2+\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(x+0)}{(2+0+0)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{x}{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349992 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349993 13194139535454 true] [17592186349992 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349994 13194139535454 true] [17592186349992 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349995 13194139535454 true] [17592186349992 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349996 13194139535454 true] [17592186349992 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349997 13194139535454 true] [17592186349992 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535454 true] [17592186349992 1041 "selection" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349992 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349993 13194139535454 true] [17592186349992 1110 #uuid "691de6ce-d5d3-5a13-9c50-06484df766