frac{2}{3}.$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350000 13194139535454 true] [17592186349999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350001 13194139535454 true] [17592186349999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350002 13194139535454 true] [17592186349999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350003 13194139535454 true] [17592186349999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350004 13194139535454 true] [17592186349999 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535454 true] [17592186349999 1041 "selection" 13194139535454 true] [17592186349999 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350001 13194139535454 true] [17592186349999 1110 #uuid "3e608aba-7cc3-5f14-9c32-5d30b1a554af" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350000 1034 "x\\ge 0" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350000 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186350000 1111 #uuid "d8d65038-7933-5b48-accc-652c62fc2c22" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350001 1034 "x\\ge \\frac{2}{3}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350001 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186350001 1111 #uuid "3e83efc3-a4a2-5c02-8a23-b7a1e0d380ed" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350002 1034 "x\\le 2" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350002 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186350002 1111 #uuid "c37427f1-19d6-5db5-b6d1-e700452a786c" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350003 1034 "x\\le \\frac{2}{3}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350003 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186350003 1111 #uuid "74fb9603-13fb-5c0b-be0d-368e1781813f" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350004 1034 "x\\ge 2" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350004 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186350004 1111 #uuid "7dae45a0-a246-5b2d-887e-38876039e3bb" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350005 1017 #edb/ref 17592186350006 13194139535454 true] [17592186350005 1089 "q-90056" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350005 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535454 true] [17592186350005 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064989/assets/2b2f637d9468aa104dff160b1ebf1f764868e14704adc02e870ea19fa12e4b17.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350005 1113 #uuid "de3c44cb-d266-5c4d-b164-e3eeaaa99800" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350005 1145 "Consider the line $x+3y=6.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{3}x+2.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies  *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" or equal to inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le -\\frac{1}{3}x+2,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+3y\\le 6.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2-x.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le 2-x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y\\le 6 \\\\ y\\le 2-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350006 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350007 13194139535454 true] [17592186350006 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350008 13194139535454 true] [17592186350006 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350009 13194139535454 true] [17592186350006 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350010 13194139535454 true] [17592186350006 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350011 13194139535454 true] [17592186350006 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535454 true] [17592186350006 1041 "selection" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350006 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350008 13194139535454 true] [17592186350006 1110 #uuid "f54292a5-bfce-5666-9990-c08fe65c74db" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350007 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x+3y<6 \\\\ y>2-x\\end{aligned}" 13194139535454 true] [17592186350007 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535454 true] [17592186350007 1111 #uuid "c84b3697-9ac6-510f-84f5-e6d0f172fa74" 13194139535454 true] [17